# Copy to .env for local dev. .env is gitignored — never commit a real one.
# In production these are set in the Vercel project settings.

# --- Browser-visible. Shipped in the JS bundle by design. ---
# Row Level Security, not secrecy, is what protects data behind these.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-supabase-publishable-or-anon-key"

# --- Server-only. Read during SSR; never exposed to the browser. ---
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-supabase-publishable-or-anon-key"

# SECURITY: the service role key bypasses Row Level Security entirely — it can
# read and write every row of every user's data. It belongs in the Vercel
# dashboard or a local .env that is never committed. If it ever lands in a
# commit, rotate it in the Supabase dashboard immediately; removing the commit
# is not enough.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

# --- Supabase Edge Function secrets. NOT app env vars. ---
# Luna and moderation run as edge functions. Set these with:
#   supabase secrets set AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...
#   AI_GATEWAY_URL       e.g. https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY   your AI provider key
#   AI_GATEWAY_MODEL     optional — defaults to a free OpenRouter model
#                        (see supabase/functions/_shared/ai.ts for how to
#                        pick a current one; free-tier slugs rotate)
#   AI_AUDIO_URL         e.g. https://api.openai.com/v1   (TTS/STT; optional)
#   AI_AUDIO_API_KEY     audio provider key               (optional)
